course: dictionary
lesson: 8225
title: Reversal: a turn to the opposite
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A reversal is a change to the opposite. The direction, the order or the result all turn the other way round, like a car that reverses back the way it came. «The South Asian monsoon is a seasonal reversal of winds: in summer moist winds blow from the Indian Ocean onto India, and in winter dry winds blow out from the land.» The winds flip direction, so reversal means a turn to the opposite.
explain: Use the context clues. The words in summer and in winter show that the wind changes direction between the two seasons. Check your meaning by putting "a complete change" in place of reversal. If the sentence still makes sense and the change goes the other way, you have it.
explain: Reversal can also mean a sudden change of luck, often from good to bad. A team that is winning can have a reversal and start losing. You may also meet "a complete reversal", when everything turns around, and "role reversal", when people swap places.
fact: Reversal is a noun: a reversal, reversals.
fact: «Reversal» means a change to the opposite direction, order or result.
fact: «Reversal» can mean a sudden change of fortune, often from good to bad.
fact: In maths, reversing ×2 with ÷2 undoes the change, so the two operations are reversals of each other.
fact: In science, melting ice and then freezing the water back to ice is a reversal of a process.
exercise: «The South Asian monsoon is a seasonal reversal of winds.» What does reversal mean here? | A place where the wind is still | A kind of rain cloud | A very loud noise | *A change to the opposite direction
exercise: In maths, reversing ×2 with ÷2 shows what? | Making a shape bigger | Adding two numbers together | *Undoing an operation | Measuring a length
exercise: A team that was winning has a reversal and starts to lose. What kind of change is this? | A quiet, calm game | A new team name | A change to a bigger score | *A sudden change of fortune from good to bad
test: «Her plan made a complete reversal when the bridge closed.» What does complete reversal suggest? | *Everything turned the other way round | A plan that was cancelled before it started | A plan that was finished early | A quiet plan with no changes
test: Which of these is a reversal of a process? | *Melting ice, then freezing the water back to ice | Drawing a circle with a compass | Counting to ten | Eating breakfast before school
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to reversal, as in a sudden turnaround? | Shade | Echo | *Turnaround | Pause
